I see my mother's face on the computer.
She smiles and greets me.
"Today after badminton, I drank tea with my new friends," I say.
"I told them the story of my arrival in Mumbai."
Mother asks, "Oh, what all did you tell them?"
"When I arrived here in January, I was a little scared," I say.
"After that, I met my new neighbour Asha."
"And I saw my colleague Rohan at the office."
Mother listens attentively; she becomes a little emotional.
"Maya, that was an important day," she says.
"Do you remember the morning of that journey?"
I nod my head.
"Yes, mother, I remember."
"Tell me that story again," mother says with love.
"That morning when you departed from Mexico."
I feel great affection in my heart.
"Okay mother, I will tell the story of that morning," I say.
We look at each other on the computer screen.
I tell the story of the start of my journey.
